      "message": "hey not clear to me where in the code are you going to use this but how about adding a node label to the gpio and using a phandle here?\n\nLike\n                i2c_b_scl: i2c_b_scl {\n                        gpios \u003d \u003c\u0026gpiob 3 GPIO_INPUT\u003e;\n                        enum-name \u003d \"GPIO_I2C_B_SCL\";\n                        label \u003d \"I2C_B_SCL\";\n                };\n\nand then use\n\nconfig {\n  sda-gpios \u003d \u003c\u0026i2c_b_scl\u003e;\n...\n}\n\nand then I think you should be able to get the enum-name property with the right macros. Advantage would be that you don\u0027t have a duplicate freetext label that needs to match in the three, but rather a pointer to it, so things would fail at compile time if there\u0027s a mismatch.\n\nIt also somewhat resembles how this would look like if were using native DT gpios here.",
